We investigate the leptoquark $U_1$ model's implications for the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, considering the constraints from $b 	o c$ transitions. We find that the model's Wilson coefficients are significantly influenced by $b 	o c$ data, which in turn affects the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$. We find that the model can accommodate the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, with a branching ratio of $10^{-7}$, and that the model's predictions for the decay's angular distribution are in good agreement with the SM.
